# Keep the Docker build context minimal and secret-free. The Dockerfile only COPYs
# pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE, and src/ — everything else is excluded here so it never
# reaches the daemon or an image layer.

# VCS and CI
.git
.github

# Local environments / secrets — MUST never enter the build context
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
tls/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# Databases and their WAL sidecars
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Python / tooling caches and build artifacts
.venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
result

# Dev-only trees not needed to build/run the image
tests/
eval/
tools/
docs/
deploy/
vulture_allowlist.py
docker-compose.yml
flake.nix
.editorconfig

# The testbed (v0.17.0). The lab drives the product over UDP and HTTP and is never imported by it;
# keeping it out of the build context is the other half of that boundary.
testbed/

# --- what `testbed/Dockerfile.ne` copies, re-included (v0.18.0, F130) -------------------------
#
# The three exclusions above hid exactly the three paths the NE image COPYs, so
# `docker compose up --build` in `testbed/` failed with `"/testbed/scenarios": not found` and
# v0.17.0 shipped an image that could not be built. `docker compose config` validates YAML and
# never reads this file, which is why nothing caught it;
# `tests/test_deploy.py::test_every_dockerfile_copy_source_survives_the_ignore_file` now does,
# by deriving the COPY sources from every Dockerfile rather than listing them here.
#
# Docker resolves the LAST matching pattern, so these three lines must stay below the two
# directory exclusions they carve out of.
#
# **What this widens, stated.** These paths now enter the build context of the *product* image
# too, which copies only `pyproject.toml`, `README.md`, `LICENSE` and `src/` — so they reach the
# daemon and no image layer. They are a PDU encoder, two agent modules and a JSON scenario: no
# secret, no credential, ~40 KB. The secret-free intent of this file is untouched; every `.env`,
# key and certificate rule above still applies, and nothing here re-includes one.
!tools/trap_replay.py
!testbed/ne
!testbed/scenarios
